    <string name="accessibility_assist_service_label">LUMO assist (off by default)</string>
    <string name="accessibility_assist_service_summary">Presses one button you name, once, when you ask</string>
    <string name="accessibility_assist_service_description">Lets LUMO press a single control that you describe, in a single app that you name, once, and only after you press a button in LUMO asking for help. It never reads or records the contents of any screen, never presses anything in permission prompts or installers, and never presses twice. Switch it off at any time; LUMO works fully without it.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_section">Accessibility assist</string>
    <string name="accessibility_intro_title">What this does, before you turn it on</string>
    <string name="accessibility_intro_body">When a page fails because the network is restricted, LUMO can open your VPN app but cannot start its tunnel — no VPN app publishes a way for another app to do that. This optional feature is the only remaining route: you describe the control in that app that means "connect", and LUMO presses it for you when you ask.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_can_title">What it can do</string>
    <string name="accessibility_can_1">Press one control, in one app, that you name by its label</string>
    <string name="accessibility_can_2">Press it once, after you press a button in LUMO</string>
    <string name="accessibility_can_3">Tell you when it could not find the control, and stop</string>
    <string name="accessibility_cannot_title">What it does not do</string>
    <string name="accessibility_cannot_1">It does not read or record anything on any screen</string>
    <string name="accessibility_cannot_2">It never presses anything in permission or install prompts</string>
    <string name="accessibility_cannot_3">It never presses twice, never repeats, never runs on its own</string>
    <string name="accessibility_cannot_4">It cannot tell whether the connection actually succeeded afterwards</string>
    <string name="accessibility_note_ack">I have read the above</string>
